## Self-verification
Before reporting work as done, prove it with this layer's real check — not
just a successful edit:
- **Check command**: `<the real command for this layer — test suite, typecheck,
  config validation, migration dry-run — from the project's actual tooling>`
- If the check fails, fix and rerun. **Budget: 3 attempts.** If still failing
  after 3, stop and report the failure honestly with the output — do not hand
  back work described as done, and do not keep burning turns.
- If the check can't run in this environment (tool missing, service down),
  say so explicitly in your report instead of skipping silently.
- **Then run every check in the playbook's Definition of done** (the command
  above is check 1). Run all, fix what failed, run all again. End your report
  with one `PASS|FAIL — <check> — evidence: <what you observed>` line per
  check and an `UNVERIFIED` list (anything you could not check, and why —
  never assume it passed). If more than two checks fail on the first pass,
  stop and name the playbook step or decision that caused it instead of
  patching the output.
- **A skipped test is not a passing test.** Report passed, failed and skipped
  counts. A test that skipped because its precondition was missing (a service,
  an env var stripped by the task runner, a database role) is unverified work:
  say which tests skipped and why. "No tests found" passes only for a package
  that genuinely has none yet.
- **Shared state isn't yours alone.** Other agents may be running at the same
  time. Don't truncate, drop, or reseed a database, cache, or queue another
  run might be using: use the isolated resource your dispatch names (a
  per-agent test database or schema, a separate port). If none was given and
  your check needs exclusive use of a shared one, say so instead of taking it.
- **Never run tree-wide git commands** (`stash`, `checkout` / `switch`,
  `reset`, `clean`, `restore`) in the shared working tree: other agents'
  uncommitted work lives there. For a baseline comparison, use
  `git worktree add <scratch dir> HEAD` and run it there.
