## Output rules
- **Report every decision the brief didn't make for you.** End your report with
  a "Decisions and assumptions" list: each choice you made that the dispatch
  didn't specify (a status code, a default, fail-open vs fail-closed, a
  library, a naming or data-shape choice) and each assumption about another
  layer. Parallel agents can't see each other's work, so an unlisted choice is
  how two reasonable halves end up incompatible.
- **Your last message is the whole report.** The orchestrator may only see your
  final message, so after a resume, a retry or a follow-up question, restate
  the complete report there (files, check results with counts, NEEDS blocks,
  decisions), not just what changed since the last message.
- **Surgical changes only** — touch what the task requires and nothing else. Don't refactor, reformat, or "improve" adjacent code that isn't broken. Match existing style even where you'd choose differently.
- **No speculative abstractions** — no config/flexibility/error-handling for scenarios nobody asked for. If a simpler version solves the actual request, ship the simpler version.
- **Clean up only your own mess** — remove imports/vars/functions your own change made unused; leave pre-existing dead code alone (mention it, don't delete it).
- **Every changed line traces to the request** — if you can't say why a line changed, it shouldn't have.
